msgid "Machine-readable output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-manager.rst:294
#: d9c68169d8514cad8c061d4918aee826
msgid ""
"The commands ``qvm-template list`` and ``qvm-template info`` provide machine-"
"readable output in both pipe(``|``)-separated and JSON format. See the ``qvm-"
"template`` man page for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-manager.rst:297
#: 83526a5a6d234c0d9a56b041386d9503
msgid "Interactions with existing tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-manager.rst:301
#: e054b5c34b14470b8df1246b44a2d959
msgid "``qvm-remove``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-manager.rst:304
#: ba443b51396b411eb00003f32857b44f
msgid ""
"The existing ``qvm-remove`` tool should behave identically to ``qvm-template "
"remove`` – albeit without fancy features like disassociation. This is unlike "
"the previous situation where ``qvm-remove`` cannot remove RPM-installed "
"templates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-manager.rst:306
#: 8406cf3ad2544cdebcb45daa3bad85d2
msgid ""
"Notably, the metadata needs no special handling as it is stored in VM "
"features and thus automatically consistent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-manager.rst:309
#: 115cf46e716e4cca8494737b103c56fb
msgid "Renaming and cloning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-manager.rst:312
#: a9aae677a4ad4ba0a1251805b7e3198a
msgid ""
"A template is treated as non-manager-installed once renamed or cloned. "
"However, relevant metadata in the VM features is still retained for future "
"extension and to serve as a hint for the user."
msgstr ""

